════ 按平台的许可形态 / Per-platform licensing ════

同一份源码在不同平台上与 sing-box 的结合方式不同，分发条款因此不同。这不是措辞选择，
是集成形态的直接后果。
The same source integrates sing-box differently per platform, so the terms
under which each artifact is distributed differ. This follows from the
integration form, not from a choice of wording.

──── 桌面（Windows / macOS / Linux）：MIT，立场未经检验 ────

Polaris 采用 mere-aggregation 立场：sing-box 以**独立子进程**运行、不与 Polaris 链接，
因此桌面产物整体仍以 MIT 发布。**该立场未经检验** —— GNU 官方 FAQ 明确「什么构成一个作品」
是法律问题，最终由法院裁定。本文件不构成法律意见。

Polaris takes the position that shipping sing-box alongside the desktop app is
mere aggregation: sing-box runs as a **separate process** and is not linked
into Polaris, so the desktop artifact stays under the MIT License. This
position is untested — the GNU FAQ states that what counts as "one work" is a
legal question ultimately decided by courts. Nothing here is legal advice.

出处 / Source: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-faq.html#MereAggregation

──── Android：GPLv3，且这一条不是灰区 ────

Android 上不存在「独立子进程」这个选项：sing-box 的 tun 入站只能经进程内的
`PlatformInterface.OpenTun` 拿到 tun 描述符（其 `TunInboundOptions` 没有接收已开 fd 的字段），
故内核以 **libbox 形态载入应用进程**，经 JNI 调用。

**因此 mere-aggregation 在 Android 上不成立，而这一条与桌面那条不同 —— 它不是一个有争议的
立场，是同进程链接的直接结果。** 不要把上面那段「未经检验」的措辞套用到本节。

此外，本仓 Android 侧的 Kotlin 实现（`src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/java/com/polaris2/app/vpn/`）
移植自 GPLv3 的 sing-box-for-android，逐文件在首行标注了上游路径：

    BoxService.kt · LocalResolver.kt · PlatformInterfaceWrapper.kt · PolarisVpnService.kt
    DefaultNetworkMonitor.kt          ← 移植（上游 https://github.com/SagerNet/sing-box-for-android）
    PolarisApplication.kt · ServiceNotification.kt   ← 结构参考
    BootstrapConfig.kt · ServiceState.kt             ← 本仓自有

**Android 产物整体按 GPLv3 分发。** Polaris 自身的源文件仍标 MIT（MIT 与 GPL 兼容），
故只取这些文件的人得到的是 MIT；而取用 Android 产物（APK）的人得到的是 GPLv3。

On Android there is no separate-process option: the tun descriptor can only be
obtained through the in-process `PlatformInterface.OpenTun`, so the kernel is
loaded into the application process as libbox and called over JNI. Mere
aggregation therefore does not apply on Android — and unlike the desktop
position above, this is not a contested reading but a direct consequence of
linking within one process. The Kotlin implementation is additionally ported
from the GPLv3 sing-box-for-android, with per-file attribution. **The Android
artifact is distributed as a whole under GPLv3.** Polaris's own source files
remain MIT-licensed (MIT is GPL-compatible), so taking those files alone gives
you MIT; taking the Android artifact gives you GPLv3.

